\ Companion module for task_load_lock_contention.1z. Its top level parks the
\ loading task mid-load: the inner task-scope body runs on a fresh task
\ context, so the sleep gate on module loads does not apply to it. The two
\ markers bracket the suspension window.

use "time" ;

"SLOW-MOD-START" print-line

[ 5 milliseconds sleep ] task-scope

"SLOW-MOD-END" print-line

slow-word: ( -- s ) [ "slow" ] ;
